@page "/slutfor/tack"
@layout MainLayout

@* The thank-you after a successful completion submission, as its own page (NFR-41). CompleteBooking
   redirects here rather than rendering the thanks as the response to its POST. As a POST response,
   Back or Reload re-sent the form; the link is single-use (FR-62), so the re-send changed nothing —
   but the guest who had just submitted was told "Uppgifterna är redan inskickade … Behöver du ändra
   något?", which reads as though something went wrong.

   The literal segment wins over CompleteBooking's /slutfor/{token} in routing, and no issued token
   can be "tack" (CompletionTokenPolicy.GenerateToken: 32 random bytes, 43 characters). The path still passes
   through TelemetryUrlRedactor, which masks the segment like a token — harmless, and the request
   name in telemetry stays the route template, so the two pages remain distinguishable there. *@

<PageTitle>Tack — Åkerögården</PageTitle>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="utility">
            <div class="utility__badge utility__badge--ok" aria-hidden="true">✓</div>
            <h1>Tack!</h1>
            <p>Dina uppgifter har skickats in. Vi hör av oss om något behöver kompletteras.</p>
            <div class="utility__actions"><a class="btn" href="/">Till startsidan</a></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
